# What a fresh install reaches with nobody having configured anything.  Most
# installs are unmanaged and stay on this list, so it has to be useful on day
# one; a managed fleet widens or narrows it by installing its own
# `/etc/exarch/net-policy.ral`, never by editing this one.
#
# `read` entries are either an exact hostname or a `*.suffix` wildcard, and
# each grants GET+HEAD only.  `write` is the whole exfiltration story: every
# host on `read` is somewhere to fetch from and nowhere to put anything, so
# a shipped default that ships with an empty `write` cannot be used to send
# a byte anywhere, whatever else it can read.  A managed fleet that trusts a
# host with uploads names it there, and names exactly the methods it means.
#
# `max-bytes` caps one response body; `rate-per-minute` caps how many
# requests this process (and everything it spawns) may make per minute.
# Both are sized for a guest that runs real installs rather than occasional
# lookups: a cap that suits a single enquiry fails a routine package fetch
# on day one.

# `search` governs the provider's own built-in web search, run server-side —
# the allowlist above cannot constrain it, since we never see the URLs it
# visits, so it gets this separate verdict.

# The `read` list is Claude Cowork's, copied wholesale: the same problem,
# solved by people who had to survive contact with real machines.  That it
# reads like a developer's list is the point — an agent does office work by
# scripting it, so PyPI and the archive are how it reaches capability the
# image does not already hold, whatever the person in front of it does for
# a living.  One host is added rather than adopted wholesale:
# `ports.ubuntu.com` is arm64 Ubuntu's real package mirror — `archive.
# ubuntu.com` alone silently starves an arm64 guest of the packages `apt`
# depends on, so leaving it off would make the default quietly useless on
# the architecture most of our guests run.

return [
  read: [
    'registry.npmjs.org', 'npmjs.com', 'www.npmjs.com', 'npmjs.org',
    'www.npmjs.org', 'yarnpkg.com', 'registry.yarnpkg.com',
    'pypi.org', 'files.pythonhosted.org', 'pythonhosted.org',
    'github.com', 'objects.githubusercontent.com',
    'archive.ubuntu.com', 'security.ubuntu.com', 'ports.ubuntu.com',
    'crates.io', 'index.crates.io', 'static.crates.io',
    'playwright.download.prss.microsoft.com', 'cdn.playwright.dev',
  ],
  write: [],
  max-bytes: 268435456,
  rate-per-minute: 240,
  search: true,
]
